{
  "title": "18: al-Kahf الكهف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَ لْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ عَلٰى عَبْدِهِ الْكِتٰبَ وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ عِوَجًا  ؕ‏(1)\nA’ZAABAN LHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE ANZALAL A’LAA A’ABDEHE KETAABA WA LAM YAJ-A’L LAHU E’EWAJAN.\nAll praise is God’s, Who sent down upon His Servant the Book (the Qur’an) and hath not caused in it any crookedness,\nقَيِّمًا لِّيُنْذِرَ بَاْسًا شَدِيْدًا مِّنْ لَّدُنْهُ وَيُبَشِّرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ اَنَّ لَهُمْ اَجْرًا حَسَنًا ۙ‏(2)\nQAYMAN LEYUNZERA BAASAN SHADEEDAA MIN LLADUNHU WAYUBASSHERA MOAMENEEN LAZEENA YA’MALOON SAALEHAATE ANNAL LAHUM AJRAN HASANAN.\n(Made it) straight that he might warn of a severe punishment from Him, and give glad tidings unto the believers who do good, that there is for them a goodly recompense,\nمّٰكِثِيْنَ فِيْهِ اَبَدًا ۙ‏(3)\nMMAAKESEENA FEEHE ABADAM.\nWherein to abide therein for ever,\nوَّيُنْذِرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ وَلَدًا‏(4)\nWWAYUNZERA LAZEENA QAALUD TAKHAZA LAAHO LAAHO.\nAnd he may warn those who say: “God hath taken unto Him a son.\nمَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ وَّلَا لِاٰبَآئِهِمْ‌ؕ كَبُرَتْ كَلِمَةً تَخْرُجُ مِنْ اَفْوَاهِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّقُوْلُوْنَ اِلَّا كَذِبًا‏(5)\nMAA LAHUM BEHI MIN I’LMIN WA LAA LEAAABAAEHEM KABURAT KALEMATAN TAKHROJO MIN AAFWAAHEHEM IN YYAQOOLOONA ILLAA KAZEBAN.\nThey have no knowledge of it nor their fathers had; grievous is the word that cometh out of their mouths; They speak not but a lie.\nفَلَعَلَّكَ بَاخِعٌ نَّفْسَكَ عَلٰٓى اٰثَارِهِمْ اِنْ لَّمْ يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ اَسَفًا‏(6)\nFALAA’ALLAKA BAAKHEA’UN NNAFSAKA A’LAA AAASAAREHEM IN LAM YOAMENOO BEHAAZAA HAAZAL AASAFAN.\nSo maybe that thou wilt worry thyself with grief after them, if they believe not in this revelation (the Qur’an).\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنَا مَا عَلَى الْاَرْضِ زِيْنَةً لَّهَا لِنَبْلُوَهُمْ اَ يُّهُمْ اَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا‏(7)\nINNAA JA-A’LNAA MAA A’LAL ARZE ZEENATAN LLAHAA LENABLOOHUM A’ZAABAN YYUHUM AHSANO A’AMALAN.\nVerily We have caused whatever is in the earth an embellishment for it, that We may test them (to prove) as to which of them is best in behaviour.\nوَاِنَّا لَجٰعِلُوْنَ مَا عَلَيْهَا صَعِيْدًا جُرُزًا ؕ‏(8)\nWA INNAA LAJAAE’ELOONA MAA A’LAYHAA SAE’EEDAN JURUZAN.\nAnd verily We will make whatever is on it bare, barren ground.\nاَمْ حَسِبْتَ اَنَّ اَصْحٰبَ الْكَهْفِ وَالرَّقِيْمِۙ كَانُوْا مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا عَجَبًا‏(9)\nAM HASEBTA ANNAL MASALAN AL-KAHFE WAALRRAQEEME KAANOO MIN AAYAATENAA A’AJABAN.\nOr thinkest thou that the fellows of the Cave and (of) the inscribe tablet (which) were of Our signs (miracles) (matters) wonderful?\nاِذْ اَوَى الْفِتْيَةُ اِلَى الْكَهْفِ فَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اٰتِنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً وَّهَيِّئْ لَنَا مِنْ اَمْرِنَا رَشَدًا‏(10)\nIZ AAWAA AL-FETYATU ELAL AL-KAHFE FA-QAALOO RABBANAA FID MIN LLADUNKA RAHMATAM WWAHAY LANAA MIN AAMRENAA RASHADAN.\nWhen sought refuge the youths unto the Cave then said they: “O’ Our Lord! Grant us mercy from unto Thee and provide for us in our affairs a right course”.\nفَضَرَبْنَا عَلٰٓى اٰذَانِهِمْ فِى الْكَهْفِ سِنِيْنَ عَدَدًا ۙ‏(11)\nFA ZARABNAA A’LAA AAZAANEHIM FIL AL-KAHFE SENEEN A’ADADAN.\nThen We did set a seal on their ears for a number of years,\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنٰهُمْ لِنَعْلَمَ اَىُّ الْحِزْبَيْنِ اَحْصٰى لِمَا لَبِثُوْۤا اَمَدًا‏(12)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAAHUM ILLAA AAA AL-HEZBAYNE AAHSAA LEMAKH MAA AAMADAN.\nThen We raised them up that We might know (i.e., show) which of the two parties reckoneth best the duration of their stay.\nنَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ نَبَاَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ فِتْيَةٌ اٰمَنُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ وَزِدْنٰهُمْ هُدًى‌ۖ‏(13)\nNAHNO NAQUSSU A’LAYKA NABAAHUM BIL-HAQ INNAHUM FETYATUN AAMANOO BE-RABBEHIM WAZEDNAAHUM HODAM.\nWe relate unto thee their story with the truth; verily, they were youths who believed in their Lord and We increased them in guidance.\nوَّرَبَطْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِذْ قَامُوْا فَقَالُوْا رَبُّنَا رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَنْ نَّدْعُوَا۫ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِلٰهًا‌ لَّقَدْ قُلْنَاۤ اِذًا شَطَطًا‏(14)\nWWARABATNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM IZ QAAMOOA FA-QAALOO RABBONAA RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAN NNADU’OOA MIN DOONEHI ELAAHANW LLAQAD QULNAL EZAL SHATATAN.\nAnd We strengthened their hearts with steadfastness, when they stood up then said they: “Our Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, Never will we call other than Him any god, for indeed then we should have uttered extravagantly.\nهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ قَوْمُنَا اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً‌ ؕ لَوْ لَا يَاْتُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍۢ بَيِّنٍ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ؕ‏(15)\nHAAOOLAAA-E QAWMUNAA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL LAW LAA YAATOONAL A’LAYHIM BESULTAANIM BAYNIN FAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN.\nThese our people have taken gods other than Him; why do they bring not a clear authority in their support? who is there more unjust than he who forges against God, a lie.\nوَاِذِ اعْتَزَلْتُمُوْهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ فَاْوٗۤا اِلَى الْكَهْفِ يَنْشُرْ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ مِّنْ رَّحْمَتِهٖ وَيُهَيِّئْ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَمْرِكُمْ مِّرْفَقًا‏(16)\nWA AA’TAZALTUMOOHUM WA MAA YA’BODOON ILLAA LAAHA FAAWA ELAL AL-KAHFE YANSHUR LAKUM RABBOKUM MIN RAHMATEHI WAYUHAY LAKUM MIN AAMREKUM MMERFAQAN.\nAnd when ye have left them and what they worship but God, betake yourselves for a refuge unto the Cave, your Lord will extend unto you His mercy, and provide for you means of (safety and) ease.\nوَتَرَى الشَّمْسَ اِذَا طَلَعَتْ تَّزٰوَرُ عَنْ كَهْفِهِمْ ذَاتَ الْيَمِيْنِ وَاِذَا غَرَبَتْ تَّقْرِضُهُمْ ذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ وَهُمْ فِىْ فَجْوَةٍ مِّنْهُ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ مَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِ ‌ۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ وَلِيًّا مُّرْشِدًا‏(17)\nWA TARAL SHAMSA EZAA TALAA’AT TTAZAAWARU A’N KAHFEHEM ZAATA YAMEENE WA EZAA GHARABAT TTAQREZUHUM ZAATA SHEMAALE WA HUM FEE FAJWATIN MINHO ZAA LEKA MIN AAYAATIL LAAHE MAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAHOWA AL-MUHTADE WA MAN YYUZLEL FALAN TAJEDA LAHU WALIYYANW MMURSHEDAN.\nAnd thou mightest see the sun, when it rose, decline from their cave unto the right and when it set, leaving them away unto the left, while they were in the cleft thereof; This is of the signs of God; Whomsoever God guideth, he is guided aright, and whomsoever He leaveth to stray, never shalt thou find for him any guide to guide (him) aright.\nوَ تَحْسَبُهُمْ اَيْقَاظًا وَّهُمْ رُقُوْدٌ ‌‌ۖ وَنُقَلِّبُهُمْ ذَاتَ الْيَمِيْنِ وَ ذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ‌‌ ۖ وَكَلْبُهُمْ بَاسِطٌ ذِرَاعَيْهِ بِالْوَصِيْدِ‌ ؕ لَوِ اطَّلَعْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَوَلَّيْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِرَارًا وَّلَمُلِئْتَ مِنْهُمْ رُعْبًا‏(18)\nWA TAHSABOHUM AAYQAAZAN WA HUM RUQOODUN WANUQALLEBUHUM ZAATA YAMEENE WA ZAATA SHEMAALE WAKALBUHUM BAASETUN ZERAAA’AYHE BIL-WASEEDE LAWE ATTALAA’TA A’LAYHIM LAWALLAYTA MINHUM FERAARAA WWALAMULETA MINHUM RUA’BAN.\nAnd thou wouldst have deemed them awake while they were asleep; and We turned them unto the right and unto the left; and their dog lay stretching his paws at the entrance, Hadst thou looked at them, surely thou wouldst have turned away from them in flight, and surely thou wouldst have been filled with awe of them.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ بَعَثْنٰهُمْ لِيَتَسَآءَلُوْا بَيْنَهُمْ‌ ؕ قَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ ؕ قَالُوْا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا اَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا رَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثْتُمْ ؕ فَابْعَثُوْۤا اَحَدَكُمْ بِوَرِقِكُمْ هٰذِهٖۤ اِلَى الْمَدِيْنَةِ فَلْيَنْظُرْ اَيُّهَاۤ اَزْكٰى طَعَامًا فَلْيَاْتِكُمْ بِرِزْقٍ مِّنْهُ وَلْيَتَلَطَّفْ وَلَا يُشْعِرَنَّ بِكُمْ اَحَدًا‏(19)\nWA KAZAALEKA BAA’ASNAAHUM LEETASAAALOOA BAYNAHUM QAALA QAAELUN MINHUM KAM LABISTUM QAALOO LABESNAA YAWMAN AW YAWM YAWMIN QAALOO RABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAA LABISTUM FAABA’ASOOA AAHADAKUM BEWAREQEKUM HAAZEHI ELAL MADEENATE FALYANZUR AYYOHAL WA TAA’AAMAN FALYAATEKUM BEREZQIN MINHO WALYATALATTAF WA LAA YUSHE’ERANNA BEKUM AHADAN.\nAnd thus did We raise them that they might question among themselves. Said one among them: “How long have ye tarried (here);” Said they: “Tarried we a day or a part of a day.” Said (the others): “Your Lord (alone) knoweth best how long ye have tarried (here); Therefore send ye then one among you with this (silver) coin of yours to the city, let him see (find out) which of them hath the purest (most whole some) food, so let him bring unto you provision from it, and let him behave gently, and maketh not you known unto any one.\nاِنَّهُمْ اِنْ يَّظْهَرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ يَرْجُمُوْكُمْ اَوْ يُعِيْدُوْكُمْ فِىْ مِلَّتِهِمْ وَلَنْ تُفْلِحُوْۤا اِذًا اَبَدًا‏(20)\nINNAHUM IN YYAZHAROOA A’LAYKUM YARJUMOOKUM AW YUE’EEDOOKUM FEE MELLATEHEM WA LAN TUFLEHOOA EZAL ABADAM.\nFor verily if they come to know of you, will stone you, or force you to return into their creed, and then never will ye succeed.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَعْثَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّاَنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا ‌ۚ اِذْ يَتَنَازَعُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْ اَمْرَهُمْ‌ فَقَالُوْا ابْنُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ بُنْيَانًا ‌ ؕ رَبُّهُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِهِمْ‌ؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ غَلَبُوْا عَلٰٓى اَمْرِهِمْ لَنَتَّخِذَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ مَّسْجِدًا‏(21)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAA’SARNAA A’LAYHIM LEEA’LAMOOA ANNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WA ANNAL SAA-A’TA LAA RAYBA FEEHAA IZ YATANAAZAU’OONA BAYNAHUM AAMRAHUM FA-QAALOO ABNOOA A’LAYHIM BUNYAANAN RABBOHUM A-A’LAMO BEHIM WA QAALA LAZEENA GHALABOOA A’LAA AMREHIM LANATTAKHEZANNA A’LAYHIM MMASJEDAN.\nAnd thus We did disclose the matter unto them (the people) that they might know that God’s promise is true, and that (about) the Hour (of Judgment) there is no doubt in it. When they disputed among themselves about the affair then said they: “Build a building (monument) over them (their cave); Their Lord knoweth them best” Those (the believers) who prevailed in their affair said: “Certainly we will have over them a Mosque.\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ ثَلٰثَةٌ رَّابِعُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ‌ۚ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ خَمْسَةٌ سَادِسُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ رَجْمًۢا بِالْغَيْبِ‌ۚ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ سَبْعَةٌ وَّثَامِنُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ‌ؕ قُلْ رَّبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِعِدَّتِهِمْ مَّا يَعْلَمُهُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ  فَلَا تُمَارِ فِيْهِمْ اِلَّا مِرَآءً ظَاهِرًا وَّلَا تَسْتَفْتِ فِيْهِمْ مِّنْهُمْ اَحَدًا‏(22)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA SALAASATUN RRAABEU’UHUM KALBUHUM WA YAQOOLOONA KHAMSATUN SAADESUHUM KALBUHUM RAJMAN BIL-GHAYBE WA YAQOOLOONA SABA’ATUN WWASAAMENUHUM KALBUHUM QUL A-A’LAMO A-A’LAMO BEE’EDDATEHEM MAA YAA’LAMUHUM ILLAA QALEELUN FALAA TUMAARE FEEHIM ILLAA MERAAAN ZAAHERAM WA LAA TASTAFTE FEEHIM MINHUM AHADAN.\n(They will) say: “(they were) Three, the fourth of them was their dog;” and say (some others): “Five, the sixth of them was their dog,” guessing about the unknown; and (yet the others) say: “seven, and the eighth of them was their dog;” Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “My Lord knoweth best their number, knoweth them not but a few;” Therefore contend not about them but a plain contention, and ask thou not any one about them.\nوَلَا تَقُوْلَنَّ لِشَاىْءٍ اِنِّىْ فَاعِلٌ ذٰ لِكَ غَدًا ۙ‏(23)\nWA LAA TAQOOLANNA LESHAAAAIN INNEE FAAE’ELUN ZAA LEKA GHADAN.\nAnd say ye not (of aught); “Verily I will do it tomorrow,\nاِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ‌ وَاذْكُرْ رَّبَّكَ اِذَا نَسِيْتَ وَقُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّهْدِيَنِ رَبِّىْ لِاَقْرَبَ مِنْ هٰذَا رَشَدًا‏(24)\nILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO WAAZKUR RRABBAKA EZAA NASEETA WA QUL A’SAA AN YYAHDEENE RABBEE LEAAQRABA MIN HAAZAA RASHADAN.\nSave (say) “If God willeth” and remember thy Lord when thou forgettest and say thou: “Maybe my Lord will guide me nearer than this to the right (way)\nوَلَبِثُوْا فِىْ كَهْفِهِمْ ثَلٰثَ مِائَةٍ سِنِيْنَ وَازْدَادُوْا تِسْعًا‏(25)\nWA MAA FEE KAHFEHEM SALAASA MEAATIN SENEEN WAAZDAADOOA TESA’AN.\nAnd stayed they in the Cave three hundred years and they add nine (more).\nقُلِ اللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثُوْا‌ ۚ لَهٗ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ اَبْصِرْ بِهٖ وَاَسْمِعْ‌ ؕ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ  وَّلَا يُشْرِكُ فِىْ حُكْمِهٖۤ اَحَدًا‏(26)\n???\nSay thou: “God (alone) knoweth best how long they stayed; His are the unseen (worlds) of the heavens and the earth; (Glory be to Him) How clear is His sight and how clear is His hearing! There is none for them other than God, any guardian, and He shareth not (with Him) in His sovereignty any one.\nوَاتْلُ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ كِتَابِ رَبِّكَ ‌ؕ لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمٰتِهٖ‌ ۚ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مُلْتَحَدًا‏(27)\n???\nAnd recite thou what hath been revealed unto thee of the Book of thy Lord; None shall change His word; And thou shalt find not other than Him, any refuge.\nوَاصْبِرْ نَفْسَكَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَدٰوةِ وَالْعَشِىِّ يُرِيْدُوْنَ وَجْهَهٗ‌ وَلَا تَعْدُ عَيْنٰكَ عَنْهُمْ‌ ۚ تُرِيْدُ زِيْنَةَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ وَ لَا تُطِعْ مَنْ اَغْفَلْنَا قَلْبَهٗ عَنْ ذِكْرِنَا وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ وَكَانَ اَمْرُهٗ فُرُطًا‏(28)\n???\nAnd restrain thou thyself with those who call unto their Lord morning and evening seeking His pleasure, and let not thy eyes turn away from them, aspiring the pomp of the life of this world; and obey not him whose heart We have made unmindful of Our remembrance, and he who followeth his inclination, and his case hath transgressed the limits.\nوَقُلِ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ‌ فَمَنْ شَآءَ فَلْيُؤْمِنْ وَّمَنْ شَآءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ ‌ۙاِنَّاۤ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ نَارًا ۙ اَحَاطَ بِهِمْ سُرَادِقُهَا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّسْتَغِيْثُوْا يُغَاثُوْا بِمَآءٍ كَالْمُهْلِ يَشْوِى الْوُجُوْهَ‌ؕ بِئْسَ الشَّرَابُ وَسَآءَتْ مُرْتَفَقًا‏(29)\nWA HAQQO MIN RABBEKUM FAMAN SHAAA-AL FALYUMEN WWAMAN SHAAA-AL FALYAKFUR INNAA A-A’TADNAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA NAARAN AHAATAL BEHIM SURAADEQUHAA WA YYASTAGHEESOOA YUGHAASOOA BE-MAAA-IM KAL-MOHL YASHWEAA AL-WUJOOHA MASALUL ASH-SHARAABU WA SAA-AT MURTAFAQAN.\nAnd say thou: “The truth is from your Lord; so let him who pleaseth believe; and let him who pleaseth disbelieve, verily We have prepared for the unjust (the Hell) fire, encompass them its enclosures; and if cry they for water, they shall be given water like the molten brass which will scald their faces; (how) wretched will be the drink; and (how) ill will be the resting place.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ اِنَّا لَا نُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ مَنْ اَحْسَنَ عَمَلًا‌ ۚ‏(30)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE INNAA LAA NUZEEU’U AJRA MAN AHSANAL A’AMALAN.\nVerily those who believe and do good deeds, verily We waste not the recompense of him who doth good deeds.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْاَنْهٰرُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيْهَا مِنْ اَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَّ يَلْبَسُوْنَ ثِيَابًا خُضْرًا مِّنْ سُنْدُسٍ وَّاِسْتَبْرَقٍ مُّتَّكِئِيْنَ فِيْهَا عَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِ‌ؕ نِعْمَ الثَّوَابُ ؕ وَحَسُنَتْ مُرْتَفَقًا‏(31)\nAOOLAAEKA LAHUM JANNAATU A’ADNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEMU ANHAARO YUHALLAWNA FEEHAA MIN ASAAWERA MIN ZAHABIN WA YALBASOONA SEEABAN KHUZRAN MIN SUNDOSINW WA ISTABRAQIM MUTTAKE-EENA FEEHAA A’LAL AL-AARAAEKE NE’MA AS-SAWAABU WAHASUNAT MURTAFAQAN.\nThese, for them are the gardens of eternity beneath which flow rivers, they shall be adorned therein with bracelets of gold, and they shall wear green robes of fine silk, and thick brocade woven with gold, reclining therein on raised couches; (What a) Blissful recompense (will it be); and (how) goodly (will be) the resting place.\nوَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ مَّثَلًا رَّجُلَيْنِ جَعَلْنَا لِاَحَدِهِمَا جَنَّتَيْنِ مِنْ اَعْنَابٍ وَّحَفَفْنٰهُمَا بِنَخْلٍ وَّجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمَا زَرْعًا ؕ‏(32)\nWAZ LAHUM MASALAM RRAJULAYNE JA-A’LNAA LEAAHADEHEMAA JANNATAYNE MIN AAA’NAABIN WWAHAFAFNAAHUMAA BENAKHLIN WA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAHOMAA ZARA’AN.\nAnd set forth unto them a parable: Two men We made for one of them two gardens of grape-vines, and We surrounded the two (gardens) with date palms, and made We corn fields in the midst of the two (gardens)\nكِلْتَا الْجَنَّتَيْنِ اٰتَتْ اُكُلَهَا وَلَمْ تَظْلِمْ مِّنْهُ شَيْئًا‌ ۙ وَّفَجَّرْنَا خِلٰلَهُمَا نَهَرًا ۙ‏(33)\nKELTAA JANNATAYNE AAATAT OKOLAHAA WA LAM TAZLEM MINHO SHAY-ANW WA FAJJARNAA KHELAALAHUMAA NAHARAN.\nBoth the gardens brought forth its fruits and failed not aught in it, and We caused a river to gush forth in their midst,\nوَكَانَ لَهٗ ثَمَرٌ‌ ۚ فَقَالَ لِصَاحِبِهٖ وَهُوَ يُحَاوِرُهٗۤ اَنَا اَكْثَرُ مِنْكَ مَالًا وَّاَعَزُّ نَفَرًا‏(34)\nKAANAL LAHU SAMARUN FAQAALA LESAAHEBEH WA HOWA YUHAAWERUH ANAA AAKSARU MENKA MAALAWN WWAAA’AZZU NAFARAN.\nAnd he had fruits (in abundance), and said he unto his companion while talking to him: “I am greater than thee in wealth and am mightier in my clan.\nوَدَخَلَ جَنَّتَهٗ وَهُوَ ظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ‌ ۚ قَالَ مَاۤ اَظُنُّ اَنْ تَبِيْدَ هٰذِهٖۤ اَبَدًا ۙ‏(35)\nWA DAKHALAL JANNATAH WA HOWA ZAALEMUN LLENAFSEH QAALA MAA AZUNNUS AN TABEEDA HAAZEHI ABADAM.\nAnd entered his garden he who was unjust to himself. Said he: “I think not that this will ever perish,\nوَّمَاۤ اَظُنُّ السَّاعَةَ قَآئِمَةً  ۙ وَّلَئِنْ رُّدِدْتُّ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ لَاَجِدَنَّ خَيْرًا مِّنْهَا مُنْقَلَبًا‏(36)\nWA MAA AZUNNUS SAA-A’TA QAAA-EMATAWN WA LA-IR RRUDEDTTU ELAA RABBEE LAAJEDANNA KHAYRAN MINHAA MUNQALABAN.\nAnd I think not that the Hour (of Resurrection and Judgment) will ever come, and even if I am returned unto my Lord, I will (ever) of a certainty find better than this a resort.\nقَالَ لَهٗ صَاحِبُهٗ وَهُوَ يُحَاوِرُهٗۤ اَكَفَرْتَ بِالَّذِىْ خَلَقَكَ مِنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ سَوّٰٮكَ رَجُلًاؕ‏(37)\nQAALA LAHU SAAHEBUH WA HOWA YUHAAWERUH AAKAFARTA BIL-LAZEE KHALAQAKA MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA SAWKA RAJULAN.\nSaid unto him his companion while talking to him: “What! disbelievest thou in Him Who created thee from dust, then from a sperm-drop, then He fashioned thee (into) a complete man?\nلّٰكِنَّا۟ هُوَ اللّٰهُ رَبِّىْ وَلَاۤ اُشْرِكُ بِرَبِّىْۤ اَحَدًا‏(38)\nLLAAKENNAA HOWA LAAHO RABBEE WA LAA AUSHREKU BE-RABBEE AHADAN.\nBut as for me He, God is my Lord, and I associate not with my Lord any one.\nوَلَوْلَاۤ اِذْ دَخَلْتَ جَنَّتَكَ قُلْتَ مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُ ۙ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ‌ ۚ اِنْ تَرَنِ اَنَا اَقَلَّ مِنْكَ مَالًا وَّوَلَدًا‌ ۚ‏(39)\nWA LAWLAA IZ DAKHALTA JANNATAKA QULTA MAA SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAA QOOTA ILLAA BIL-LAAHE IN TARANE ANAA AAQALLA MENKA MAALAWN WWAWALADAN.\nAnd why didst thou not say when thou didst enter thy garden: “(It is) as God willeth! there is no power but with God, if thou dost see me less than thee in wealth and children.\nفَعَسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَنْ يُّؤْتِيَنِ خَيْرًا مِّنْ جَنَّتِكَ وَيُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهَا حُسْبَانًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فَتُصْبِحَ صَعِيْدًا زَلَقًا ۙ‏(40)\nFA A’SAA RABBEE AN YYUTEENE KHAYRAN MIN JANNATEKA WAYURSELA A’LAYHAA HUSBAANAN MENAL SAMAAA-E FATUSBEHA SAE’EEDAN ZALAQAN.\nYet maybe my Lord may give me better than thy garden, and send on it (on thy garden) thunderbolts (as a reckoning) from heaven, that it becometh barren slippery dust,\nاَوْ يُصْبِحَ مَآؤُهَا غَوْرًا فَلَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعَ لَهٗ طَلَبًا‏(41)\nAW YUSBEHA MAAUHAA GHAWRAN FALAN TASTATEEA’A LAHU TALABAN.\nOr get sunk underground its waters and thereafter never thou art able to search for it.\nوَاُحِيْطَ بِثَمَرِهٖ فَاَصْبَحَ يُقَلِّبُ كَفَّيْهِ عَلَىٰ مَاۤ اَنْفَقَ فِيْهَا وَهِىَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلٰى عُرُوْشِهَا وَيَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اُشْرِكْ بِرَبِّىْۤ اَحَدًا‏(42)\nWAAHEETA BE-SAMAREHI FA ASBAHA YUQALLEBU KAFFAYHE A’LAA MAA AANFAQA FEEHAA WA HEYA KHAAWEYATUN A’LAA O’ROOSHEEHAA WA YAQOOLO YAA LAYTANEE LAM AUSHREK BE-RABBEE AHADAN.\nAnd his fruits were enwrapped into destruction, so he began wringing his hands for what he had spent in it, and it (his garden) lay fallen on its roofs, and said he: “Alas me! Would that I had not associated with my Lord any one!\nوَلَمْ تَكُنْ لَّهٗ فِئَةٌ يَّنْصُرُوْنَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا كَانَ مُنْتَصِرًا ؕ‏(43)\nWA LAM TAKUN LAHU FEATUN YANSOROONAHU MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA MAA KAANA MUNTASERAN.\nHe had no force to help him other than God, nor could he himself help.\nهُنَالِكَ الْوَلَايَةُ لِلّٰهِ الْحَقِّ‌ؕ هُوَ خَيْرٌ ثَوَابًا وَّخَيْرٌ عُقْبًا‏(44)\nHONAALEKAB AL-WALAAYATU LILLAAHE HAQQ HOWA KHAYRUL SAWAABAN WWAKHAYRUN U’UQBAN.\nHere (in the event of such a helplessness) protection is only God’s the Truth; He is the Best to reward and the Best to requite.\nوَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ مَّثَلَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا كَمَآءٍ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ فَاخْتَلَطَ بِهٖ نَبَاتُ الْاَرْضِ فَاَصْبَحَ هَشِيْمًا تَذْرُوْهُ الرِّيٰحُ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّقْتَدِرًا‏(45)\nWAZ LAHUM MMASALA HAYAATID DUNYAA KA-MAAA-IM ANZALNAAHO MENAL SAMAAA-E FAAKHTALATA BEHI NABAATU ARZE FA ASBAHA HASHEEMAN TAZROOHU AR-REEHU KAANAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN MMUQTADERAN.\nAnd set thou unto them the similitude of the life of this world, like the water which send We down from heaven, and the herbage of the earth mingleth with it, then it becometh dry stubble which the winds scatter; for God over all things hath power.\nاَلْمَالُ وَ الْبَنُوْنَ زِيْنَةُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ وَالْبٰقِيٰتُ الصّٰلِحٰتُ خَيْرٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابًا وَّخَيْرٌ اَمَلًا‏(46)\nAALMAALU WA AL-BANOONA ZEENATU HAYAATID DUNYAA WAL BAAQEETU AS-SAALEHAATU KHAYRUL I’NDAL RABBEKA SAWAABAN WWAKHAYRUN AAMALAN.\nWealth and children are the adornment of the life of this world; and the everlasting good works are best in view of thy Lord in (earning the) reward, and best as hopes (of His mercy).\nوَيَوْمَ نُسَيِّرُ الْجِبَالَ و تَرَى الْاَرْضَ بَارِزَةً  ۙ وَّحَشَرْنٰهُمْ فَلَمْ نُغَادِرْ مِنْهُمْ اَحَدًا‌ ۚ‏(47)\nWA YAWMA NUSAYRU JEBAALA W TARAL ARZA BAAREZATAN WWAHASHARNAAHUM FALAM NUGHAADER MINHUM AHADAN.\nAnd the day when We will cause the mountains to pass away, and thou seest the earth a levelled plain and We will gather them (and) then leave not behind, of them any one.\nوَعُرِضُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّكَ صَفًّا ؕ لَقَدْ جِئْتُمُوْنَا كَمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ۢ  بَلْ زَعَمْتُمْ اَ لَّنْ نَّجْعَلَ لَكُمْ مَّوْعِدًا‏(48)\nWAU’UREZOOA A’LAA RABBEKA MALAAA-EKATO LAQAD JETUMOONAA KAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM AWWALA MARRAH BAL ZA-A’MTUM A’ZAABAN LAN-Y NNAJA’ALA LAKUM MMAWE’EDAN.\nAnd they shall set before thy Lord in ranks; (and it will be said unto them): “Now are ye come unto Us as We created you at first: and yet ye thought never We had made unto you a tryst.\nوَوُضِعَ الْكِتٰبُ فَتَرَى الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ مُشْفِقِيْنَ مِمَّا فِيْهِ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ يٰوَيْلَتَنَا مَالِ هٰذَا الْكِتٰبِ لَا يُغَادِرُ صَغِيْرَةً وَّلَا كَبِيْرَةً اِلَّاۤ اَحْصٰٮهَا‌ ۚ وَوَجَدُوْا مَا عَمِلُوْا حَاضِرًا‌ ؕ وَ لَا يَظْلِمُ رَبُّكَ اَحَدًا‏(49)\nWAWUZEA’A KETAABO FATARAL MUJREMEEN MUSHFEQEENA MIMMAA FEEHE WA YAQOOLOONA YAAWAYLATANAA MAALE HAAZAA KETAABE LAA YUGHAADERU SAGHEERATAN WA LAA KABEERATAN ILLAA AAHSAAHAA WAWAJADOOA MAA A’MELOO HAAZERAN WA LAA YAZLEMU RABBOKA AHADAN.\nAnd (when) the Book of (deeds) is placed then wilt thou see the guilty, dreadful of what is (recorded) in it: and they will say: “Ah woe unto us! What a book is this! it leaveth not aught (of our sins) small or great but enumereth (each one of) them!” And will find they what ever they did, present (in it): and dealeth not thy Lord unjustly with any one.\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ كَانَ مِنَ الْجِنِّ فَفَسَقَ عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهٖؕ اَفَتَتَّخِذُوْنَهٗ وَذُرِّيَّتَهٗۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِىْ وَهُمْ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ ؕ بِئْسَ لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَدَلًا‏(50)\nWA IZ QULNAL LIL-MALAAEKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA IBLEES KAANA MENAL JINNE FAFASAQA A’N AMRE RABBEH AAFATATTAKHEZOONAH WAZURREETAH AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONEAA WA HUM LAKUM A’DUWWUM MASALUL LIZ-ZAALEMEENA BADALAN.\nAnd when said We unto the angels: “Prostrate ye unto Adam!” then they (all) prostrated but ‘Iblis’; he was of the jinn, and he transgressed the behest of his Lord; What! would ye then take him and his progeny as friends rather than Me, and they are enemies unto you! Evil for the unjust would be the exchange.\nمَّاۤ اَشْهَدْتُّهُمْ خَلْقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلَا خَلْقَ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَمَا كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذَ الْمُضِلِّيْنَ عَضُدًا‏(51)\nMAA AASHHADTTUHUM KHALQA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LAA KHALQA ANFOSEHIM WA MAA KUNTO MUTTAKHEZA AL-MUZELLEENA A’AZUDAN.\nI called them not to witness the creation of the heavens and the earth, nor of the creation of their selves; nor am I he who taketh those who lead (people) astray, as helpers.\nوَيَوْمَ يَقُوْلُ نَادُوْا شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ فَدَعَوْهُمْ فَلَمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَهُمْ وَجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ مَّوْبِقًا‏(52)\nWA YAWMA YAQOOLO NAADOOA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM FADA-A’WHUM FALAM YASTAJEEBOO LAHUM WA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAHUM MMAWBEQAN.\nAnd the Day (of Judgment) when He will say: “Call ye on those whom ye thought to be my partners,” and they will call on them, but they will not listen to them, and We will cause between them a valley of perdition.\nوَرَاَ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ النَّارَ فَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ مُّوَاقِعُوْهَا وَ لَمْ يَجِدُوْا عَنْهَا مَصْرِفًا‏(53)\nWA RA-AL MUJREMOON NAARAL FAZANNOOA ANNAHUM MMOOAQEU’OOHAA WA LAM YAJEDOOA A’NHAA MASREFAN.\nAnd shall see the guilty ones the fire, and apprehend that they are falling into it, and they will find not any escape thence.\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لِلنَّاسِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ اَكْثَرَ شَىْءٍ جَدَلًا‏(54)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA FEE HAAZAA QUR-AANE LIN-NAASE MIN KULLE MASALIN KAANAL INSAANO AKSARAN SHAY-IN JADALAN.\nAnd indeed have We (fully) displayed for mankind in this Qur’an every kind of similitude; but man, of most things, is contentious.\nوَمَا مَنَعَ النَّاسَ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْۤا اِذْ جَآءَهُمُ الْهُدٰى وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ سُنَّةُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ اَوْ يَاْتِيَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ قُبُلًا‏(55)\nWA MAA MANAA’A NAASA AN YOAMENOO IZ JAAA-AHOMUL HODAA WAYASTAGHFEROOA RABBAHUM ILLAA AN TAATEEHUM SUNNATU AWWALEEN AW YAATEEHUMU A’ZAABO QUBULAN.\nAnd nothing preventeth the people from believing when the guidance came unto them, and from asking for the forgiveness from their Lord except overtaketh them, the fate of the ancients or cometh face to face unto them the chastisement.\nوَمَا نُرْسِلُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَ‌ ۚ وَيُجَادِلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ لِيُدْحِضُوْا بِهِ الْحَقَّ‌ وَاتَّخَذُوْۤا اٰيٰتِىْ وَمَاۤ اُنْذِرُوْا هُزُوًا‏(56)\nWA MAA NURSELU MURSALEEN ILLAA MOBASH-SHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN WAYUJAADELU LAZEENA KAFAROO BIL-BAATELE LEEDHEZOOA BEHIL HAQQA WAT-TAKHAZOO AAAYAATEAA WA MAA AUNZEROOA HOZOWANW.\nAnd We send not apostles but as bearers of glad tidings and warners; and dispute those who disbelieve with falsehood that they may refute with it the truth, and take they My signs and that they have been warned with, for a jest.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ ذُكِّرَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ فَاَعْرَضَ عَنْهَا وَنَسِىَ مَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰهُ‌ ؕ اِنَّا جَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ تَدْعُهُمْ اِلَى الْهُدٰى فَلَنْ يَّهْتَدُوْۤا اِذًا اَبَدًا‏(57)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMAN ZUKKERA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHI FA-A’RAZA A’NHAA WANASEAAA MAA QADDAMAT YADAAHO INNAA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AAKENNATAN AN YYAFQAHOOHU WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAN WA TADU’UHUM ELAL HODAA FALAN YYAHTADOOA EZAL ABADAM.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who is reminded of the signs of his Lord, then he turneth away from them and forgetteth what have sent forth his two hands? Verily We have caused veils over their hearts lest they understand it and in their ears a heaviness; And if thou calleth them unto guidance, never will they in that case get guided aright at all.\nوَرَبُّكَ الْغَفُوْرُ ذُوْ الرَّحْمَةِ‌ ؕ لَوْ يُؤَاخِذُهُمْ بِمَا كَسَبُوْا لَعَجَّلَ لَهُمُ الْعَذَابَ‌ ؕ بَلْ لَّهُمْ مَّوْعِدٌ لَّنْ يَّجِدُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مَوْئِلًا‏(58)\nWA RABBOKA GHAFOORUL ZOO AR-RAHMATE LAW YUAAKHEZUHUM BEMAA KASABOO LAA’AJJALA LAHOMUL A’ZAABA BAL LAHUM MMAWE’EDUN LAN-Y YYAJEDOOA MIN DOONEHI MAWELAN.\nAnd thy Lord is Oft-Forgiving and the Lord of Mercy; were He to seize them for what they earn, surely He would have hastened for them the chastisement; but for them is a tryst never shall they find, besides it, a refuge.\nوَتِلْكَ الْقُرٰٓى اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ لَمَّا ظَلَمُوْا وَجَعَلْنَا لِمَهْلِكِهِمْ مَّوْعِدًا‏(59)\nWA TILKAL QORAA AHLAKNAAHUM LAMMAA ZALAMOO WA JA-A’LNAA LEMAHLEKEHEM MMAWE’EDAN.\nAnd these towns, We did destroy them when they committed iniquities; but We had a tryst for their destruction.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِفَتٰٮهُ لَاۤ اَبْرَحُ حَتّٰۤى اَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ اَوْ اَمْضِىَ حُقُبًا‏(60)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LEFATAAHU LAA AABRAHU HATTAA AABLUGHA MAJMAA’A WA AW AAMZEAAA HUQUBAN.\nAnd (remember) when said Moses unto his boy: “I will cease not until I reach the junction of the two rivers or I will go on (a non-stop march) for years.\nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا نَسِيَا حُوْتَهُمَا فَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيْلَهٗ فِى الْبَحْرِ سَرَبًا‏(61)\nFALAMMAA BALAGHAA MAJMAA’A BAYNEHEMAA NASEEA HOOTAHUMAA FA TAKHAZA SABEELAH FIL BAHRE SARABAN.\nSo when they reached the junction of the two (rivers), they forgot their fish and it took its way into the sea making a hole (in the earth).\nفَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتٰٮهُ اٰتِنَا غَدَآءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِيْنَا مِنْ سَفَرِنَا هٰذَا نَصَبًا‏(62)\nFALAMMAA JAAWAZAA QAALA LEFATAAHU FID GHADAAANAA LAQAD LAQEENAA MIN SAFARENAA HAAZAA NASABAN.\nBut when they had gone (some distance) said he unto his boy “Bring unto us our morning meal, indeed we have met from this our journey weariness.\nقَالَ اَرَءَيْتَ اِذْ اَوَيْنَاۤ اِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ فَاِنِّىْ نَسِيْتُ الْحُوْتَ وَ مَاۤ اَنْسٰٮنِيْهُ اِلَّا الشَّيْطٰنُ اَنْ اَذْكُرَهٗ‌ ‌ۚ وَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيْلَهٗ فِىْ الْبَحْر‌ِ ‌ۖ عَجَبًا‏(63)\nQAALA A-RA-AYTA IZ AAWAYNAA ELAL AS-SAKHRATE FA-INNEE NASEETU AL-HOOTA WA MAA AANSAANEEHU ILLAA SHAYTAANO AN AAZKURAH WA TAKHAZA SABEELAH FEE BAHRE A’AJABAN.\nHe said: “Didst thou see (what happened) when we took refuge on the rock, then verily I forgot the fish, and nothing made me forget to mention of it but the devil; and it took its way into the sea, what a wonder it is!\nقَالَ ذٰ لِكَ مَا كُنَّا نَبْغِ ‌‌ۖ  فَارْتَدَّا عَلٰٓى اٰثَارِهِمَا قَصَصًا ۙ‏(64)\nQAALA ZAA LEKA MAA KUNNAA NABGHE FAARTADDAA A’LAA AAASAAREHEMAA QASASAN.\nHe said: “That is (the place) what we were seeking for!” So they retraced their steps,\nفَوَجَدَا عَبْدًا مِّنْ عِبَادِنَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا وَعَلَّمْنٰهُ مِنْ لَّدُنَّا عِلْمًا‏(65)\nFAWAJADAA A’BDAN MIN E’EBAADENAA AATAYNAAHO RAHMATAM MIN I’NDENAA WA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA MIN WA I’LMAN.\nThen found they one, from among Our servants whom We had vouchsafed mercy from unto Us and We had taught him knowledge unto Ourselves.\nقَالَ لَهٗ مُوْسٰى هَلْ اَتَّبِعُكَ عَلٰٓى اَنْ تُعَلِّمَنِ مِمَّا عُلِّمْتَ رُشْدًا‏(66)\nQAALA LAHU MOOSAA HAL AATTABEU’UKA A’LAA AN TUA’ALLEMANE MIMMAA U’ULLEMTA RUSHDAN.\nSaid unto him Moses: “Shall I follow thee on condition that thou shouldst teach me aright of what thou hast been taught.\nقَالَ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعَ مَعِىَ صَبْرًا‏(67)\nQAALA INNAKA LAN TASTATEEA’A MA-E’YA SABRANW.\nSaid he: “Verily, thou canst not have patience with me.\nوَكَيْفَ تَصْبِرُ عَلٰى مَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهٖ خُبْرًا‏(68)\nWA KAYFA TASBERU A’LAA MAA LAM TOHIT BEHI KHUBRAN.\nHow canst thou be patient about what thou comprehendest not its knowledge.\nقَالَ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ صَابِرًا وَّلَاۤ اَعْصِىْ لَكَ اَمْرًا‏(69)\nQAALA SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO SAABERAN WA LAA AAA’SEAA LAKA AMRAN.\nHe said: “Thou wilt find me patient if God willeth, and I shall not disobey thee in any matter.\nقَالَ فَاِنِ اتَّبَعْتَنِىْ فَلَا تَسْئَلْنِىْ عَنْ شَىْءٍ حَتّٰٓى اُحْدِثَ لَكَ مِنْهُ ذِكْرًا‏(70)\nQAALA FA-ENIN ATTABAA’TANEAA FALAA TASALNEAA A’N SHAY-IN HATTAA AUHDESA LAKA MINHO ZIKRAA.\nSaid he: “If thou followest me, ask me not of aught until I myself unto thee make mention of it.\nفَانْطَلَقَا حَتّٰۤى اِذَا رَكِبَا فِى السَّفِيْنَةِ خَرَقَهَا‌ ؕ قَالَ اَخَرَقْتَهَا لِتُغْرِقَ اَهْلَهَا‌ ۚ لَقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا اِمْرًا‏(71)\nFAANTALAQAA HATTAA EZAA RAKEBAA FIL SAFEENATE WA KHARAQAHAA QAALA AAKHARAQTAHAA LETUGHREQA JA-A’LA LAQAD BIL-HAQ SHAY-ANW AEMRAN.\nThen they went (their way) until they embarked in the boat, he made a hole in it. (Moses) said: “Made thee a hole in it to drown its inmates? Indeed thou hast done a strange thing?\nقَالَ اَلَمْ اَقُلْ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعَ مَعِىَ صَبْرًا‏(72)\nQAALA ALAM AAQUL INNAKA LAN TASTATEEA’A MA-E’YA SABRANW.\nHe said: “Said I not unto thee that thou canst not be with me in patience?\nقَالَ لَا تُؤَاخِذْنِىْ بِمَا نَسِيْتُ وَلَا تُرْهِقْنِىْ مِنْ اَمْرِىْ عُسْرًا‏(73)\nQAALA LAA TUAAKHEZNEAA BEMAA NASEETU WA LAA TURHEQNEAA MIN AMREE U’USRAN.\nSaid he (Moses): “Chide me not that I forgot, and constrain me not to a difficulty in my affair.\nفَانْطَلَقَاحَتّٰۤى اِذَا لَقِيَا غُلٰمًا فَقَتَلَهٗ ۙ قَالَ اَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا زَكِيَّةً ۢ بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ ؕ لَقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا نُّكْرًا‏(74)\nFAANTALAQAAHATTAA EZAA LAQEEA GHULAAMAN FAQATALAH QAALA AAQATALTA NAFSAN ZAKEETAN BEGHAYRIL NAFSIM LAQAD BIL-HAQ SHAY-ANW NUKRAA.\nThen they went on until they met a boy, he slew him. Said (Moses): “Slew thou an innocent person, who had slain none? Indeed thou hast done a horrible thing!\nقَالَ اَ لَمْ اَ قُلْ لَّكَ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعَ مَعِىَ صَبْرًا‏(75)\nQAALA ALAM AQUL LAKA INNAKA LAN TASTATEE-A’ MA-E’YA SABRAN.\nHe said: “Said I not unto thee that thou couldst not be with me in patience?\nقَالَ اِنْ سَاَ لْتُكَ عَنْ شَىْءٍۢ بَعْدَهَا فَلَا تُصٰحِبْنِىْ‌ ۚ قَدْ بَلَغْتَ مِنْ لَّدُنِّىْ عُذْرًا‏(76)\nQAALA IN SA-ALTOKA A’N SHAY-IM BA’-DAHAA FALAA TOSAHEBNEE QAD BALAGHTA MIL LADUNNEE U’ZRAN.\nSaid he: “If ever I ask thee about anything after this, then suffer me not to be in thy company; then indeed thou hast had an excuse (to do so) unto me.\nفَانْطَلَقَا حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَتَيَاۤ اَهْلَ قَرْيَةِ  ۨاسْتَطْعَمَاۤ اَهْلَهَا فَاَبَوْا اَنْ يُّضَيِّفُوْهُمَا فَوَجَدَا فِيْهَا جِدَارًا يُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّنْقَضَّ فَاَقَامَهٗ‌ ؕ قَالَ لَوْ شِئْتَ لَتَّخَذْتَ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا‏(77)\nFANTALAQAA HATTAA EZAA ATAYAA AHLA QARYATENIS TATA’-MAA AHLAHAA FA-ABAW ANY YOZAYYEFOOHOMAA FA-WAJADAA FEEHAA JEDAARANY YOREEDO ANY YANQAZZA FA-AQAAMAH, QAALA LAW SHE-TA LATTAKHAZTA A’LAYHE AJRAN.\nThen went they on until they came to the people of a town, they asked its people for food, but they declined to receive them as (their) guests, then they found in it (the town) a wall about to fall, and he set it upright. Said he: “If thou hadst wished, thou mightest surely have taken a return (payment) for it ”.\nقَالَ هٰذَا فِرَاقُ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنِكَ‌‌ ۚ سَاُنَبِّئُكَ بِتَاْوِيْلِ مَا لَمْ تَسْتَطِعْ عَّلَيْهِ صَبْرًا‏(78)\nQAALA HAAZAA FERAAQO BAYNEE WA BAYNEKA, SA-ONABBE-OKA BE-TAA-WEELE MAA LAM TASTATE’ A’LAYHE SABRAN.\nHe said: “This shall be the parting point between me and thee, now I will acquaint thee of the interpretation of what thou couldst not bear with patience.\nاَمَّا السَّفِيْنَةُ فَكَانَتْ لِمَسٰكِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ فِى الْبَحْرِ فَاَرَدْتُّ اَنْ اَعِيْبَهَا وَكَانَ وَرَآءَهُمْ مَّلِكٌ يَّاْخُذُ كُلَّ سَفِيْنَةٍ غَصْبًا‏(79)\nAMMAS SAFEENATO FA-KAANAT LEMASAAKEENA YA’-MALOONA FIL BAHRE FA-ARADTO AN A-E’EBAHAA WA KAANA WARAAA-AHOM MALEKUY YAA-KHOZO KULLA SAFEENATIN GHASBAA.\nAs for the boat, it was of (some) poor men they plied in the sea and I intended that I should damage it, for there was after them a king who seized every boat by force\nوَاَمَّا الْغُلٰمُ فَكَانَ اَبَوٰهُ مُؤْمِنَيْنِ فَخَشِيْنَاۤ اَنْ يُّرْهِقَهُمَا طُغْيَانًا وَّكُفْرًا‌ۚ‏(80)\nWA AMMAL GHOLAAMO FA-KAANA ABAWAAHO MO-MENAYNE FA-KHASHEENAA AN YURHEQAHOMAA TUGHYAANAW WA KUFRAN.\nAnd as for the boy, because his parents are believers and feared we that he should grieve them by rebellion (against them) and disbelieve (in God).\nفَاَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ يُّبْدِلَهُمَا رَبُّهُمَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهُ زَكٰوةً وَّاَقْرَبَ رُحْمًا‏(81)\nFA-ARADNAA AY YUBDELAHOMAA RABBOHOMAA KHAYRAM MINHO ZAKAATANW WA AQRABA ROHMAA.\nSo we did intend that their Lord giveth them instead one better than him in purity (of conduct) and closer in affection.\nوَاَمَّا الْجِدَارُ فَكَانَ لِغُلٰمَيْنِ يَتِيْمَيْنِ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ وَكَانَ تَحْتَهٗ كَنْزٌ لَّهُمَا وَكَانَ اَبُوْهُمَا صَالِحًا ۚ فَاَرَادَ رَبُّكَ اَنْ يَّبْلُغَاۤ اَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسْتَخْرِجَا كَنْزَهُمَا ۖ  رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌‌ ۚ وَمَا فَعَلْتُهٗ عَنْ اَمْرِىْ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ تَاْوِيْلُ مَا لَمْ تَسْطِعْ عَّلَيْهِ صَبْرًا ؕ‏(82)\nWA AMMAL JEDAARO FA-KAANA LE-GHOLAAMAYNE YATEEMAYNE FIL MEDEENATE WA KAANA TAHTAHU KANZUL LAHOMAA WA KAANA ABOOHOMAA SAALEHAN FA-ARAADA RABBOKA AY YABLOGHAA ASHUDDAHOMAA WA YASTAKHREJAA KANZAHOMAA RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA WA MAA FA-A’LTOHU A’N AMREE ZAALEKA TAA-WEELO MAA LAM TASTE’ A’LAYHE SABRAA.\nAnd as for the wall, it was of two orphan boys in the city, and was underneath it (depo-sited) a treasure (intended) for them two and their father was a righteous man; so willed thy Lord that they should attain their maturity and take out their treasure (which is) a mercy from thy Lord; and I did it not of my own will. This is the interpretation of what thou couldst not have patience.\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنْ ذِى الْقَرْنَيْنِ‌ ؕ قُلْ سَاَ تْلُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْهُ ذِكْرًا ؕ‏(83)\nWA YAS-ALOONAKA A’N ZIL QARNAYNE, QUL SA-ATLOO A’LAYKUM MINHO ZIKRAA.\nAnd they ask thee about Dhu al-Qarnayn. Say thou: “I shall recite unto you of him a mention.\nاِنَّا مَكَّنَّا لَهٗ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ سَبَبًا ۙ‏(84)\nINNAA MAKKANNAA LAHU FIL ARZE WA AATAYNAAHO MIN KULLE SHAY-IN SABABAA.\n(Sayeth the Lord) Verily We did make him mighty in the earth, and We gave him the means of access to every thing,\nفَاَ تْبَعَ سَبَبًا‏(85)\nFA-ATBA-A’ SABABAA.\nSo followed he a route.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا بَلَغَ مَغْرِبَ الشَّمْسِ وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِىْ عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍ وَّوَجَدَ عِنْدَهَا قَوْمًا ؕ ‌قُلْنَا يٰذَا الْقَرْنَيْنِ اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُعَذِّبَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ تَتَّخِذَ فِيْهِمْ حُسْنًا‏(86)\nHATTAA EZAA BALAGHA MAGHREBASH SHAMSE WAJADAHAA TAGHROBO FEE A’YNIN HAME-ATIW WA WAJADA I’NDAHAA QAWMAA, QULNAA YAA ZAL QARNAYNE IMMAA AN TO-A’ZZEBA WA IMMAA AN TATTAKHEZA FEEHIM HUSNAA.\nUntil when he reached the place where settest the sun (the Western most land) and found it (the sun) setting in a black muddy pool, and found by it a people. Said We: “O’ Dhu al-Qarnayn! Either chastise them thou (for their infidelity) or treat them with kindness (if they correct themselves).\nقَالَ اَمَّا مَنْ ظَلَمَ فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهٗ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ فَيُعَذِّبُهٗ عَذَابًا نُّكْرًا‏(87)\nQAALA AMMAA MAN ZALAMA FA-SAWFA NO-A’ZZEBOHU SUMMA YORADDO ELAA RABBEHI FA-YO-A’ZZEBOHU A’ZAABAN NUKRAA.\n(And) said He: “As to him who is unjust We will chastise him, then he shall be returned unto his Lord, and He will chastise him with a grievous chastisement.\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلَهٗ جَزَآءَ  ۨالْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ وَسَنَقُوْلُ لَهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِنَا يُسْرًا ؕ‏(88)\nWA AMMAA MAN AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-LAHU JAZAAA-A NIL HUSNAA, WA SANAQOOLO LAHU MIN AMRENAA YUSRAA.\nAnd as for him who believeth and doeth good, for him shall be a goodly recompense; and We will speak unto him (only) of easy (one of) Our command.\nثُمَّ اَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا‏(89)\nSUMMA ATBA-A’ SABABAA.\nThen he followed (another) route.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَابَلَغَ مَطْلِعَ الشَّمْسِ وَجَدَهَا تَطْلُعُ عَلٰى قَوْمٍ لَّمْ نَجْعَلْ لَّهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهَا سِتْرًا ۙ‏(90)\nHATTAA EZAA BALAGHA MATLE-A’SH SHAMSE WAJADAHAA TATLO-O’ A’LAA QAWMIL LAM NAJ-A’L LAHUM MIN DOONEHAA SITRAA.\nUntil when he reached the place where riseth the sun, he found it rising on a people for whom We had provided not any shelter,\nكَذٰلِكَؕ وَقَدْ اَحَطْنَا بِمَا لَدَيْهِ خُبْرًا‏(91)\nKAZAALEKA WA QAD AHATNAA BEMAA LADAYHE KHUBRAA.\nEven so; and indeed We had full knowledge of whatever was with him.\nثُمَّ اَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا‏(92)\nSUMMA ATBA-A’ SABABAA.\nThen he followed (another) route.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا بَلَغَ بَيْنَ السَّدَّيْنِ وَجَدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمَا قَوْمًا ۙ لَّا يَكَادُوْنَ يَفْقَهُوْنَ قَوْلًا‏(93)\nHATTAA EZAA BALAGHA BAYNAS SADDAYNE WAJADA MIN DOONEHEMAA QAWMAL LAA YAKAADOONA YAFQAHOONA QAWLAA.\nUntil when he reached between two mountains he found on the hither side of the two (mountains) a people who could scarce understand a word.\nقَالُوْا يٰذَا الْقَرْنَيْنِ اِنَّ يَاْجُوْجَ وَمَاْجُوْجَ مُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا عَلٰٓى اَنْ تَجْعَلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ سَدًّا‏(94)\nQAALOO YAA ZAL QARNAYNE INNA YAA-JOOJA WA MAA-JOOJA MUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE FA-HAL NAJ-A’LO LAKA KHARJAN A'LAA AN TAJ-A'LA BAYNANAA WA BAYNAHUM SADDAA.\nSaid they: ‘O’ Dhu al-Qarnayn! Verily Gog and Magog cause mischief in the land, shall we collect for thee the (necessary) resources (from among ourselves) so that thou shalt raise between us and them a barrier?\nقَالَ مَا مَكَّنِّىْ فِيْهِ رَبِّىْ خَيْرٌ فَاَعِيْنُوْنِىْ بِقُوَّةٍ اَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا ۙ‏(95)\nQAALA MAA MAKKANNEE FEEHE RABBEE KHAYRUN FA-A-E’ENOONEE BE-QUWWATIN AJ-A’L BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM RADMAA.\nHe said: “The power in which hath my Lord established me is better, so ye help me only with the strength (of labourers), I will make between you and them a barrier,\nاٰتُوْنِىْ زُبَرَ الْحَدِيْدِ‌ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا سَاوٰى بَيْنَ الصَّدَفَيْنِ قَالَ انْفُخُوْا‌ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَعَلَهٗ نَارًا ۙ قَالَ اٰتُوْنِىْۤ اُفْرِغْ عَلَيْهِ قِطْرًا ؕ‏(96)\nAATOONEE ZOBARAL HADEEDE HATTAA EZAA SAAWAA BAYNAS SADAFAYNE QAALANFOKHOO, HATTAA EZAA JA-A’LAHU NAARAN QAALA AATOONEE UFRIGH A’LAYHE QITRAA.\nBring ye unto me blocks of iron,” until when it filled the space between the mountain sides, said he: “Ply your bellows,” until he had made it red-hot with fire, he said: “Bring unto me molten brass which I may pour over it.\nفَمَا اسْطَاعُوْۤا اَنْ يَّظْهَرُوْهُ وَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا لَهٗ نَقْبًا‏(97)\nFAMAS-TAA-O’O ANY YAZHAROOHO WA MASTA-TAA-O’O LAHU NAQBAA.\nSo they could not scale it nor could they make a hole in it.\nقَالَ هٰذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ‌ ۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّىْ جَعَلَهٗ دَكَّآءَ‌ ۚ وَكَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّىْ حَقًّا ؕ‏(98)\nQAALA HAAZAA RAHMATUM MIR RABBEE FA-EZAA JAAA-A WA’-DO RABBEE JA-A’LAHU DAKKAAA-A, WA KAANA WA’-DO RABBEE HAQQAA.\nSaid he: “This is a mercy from my Lord; but when the promise of my Lord (the Resurrection) cometh to pass, He will level it with the ground; and the promise of my Lord is (always) true.\nوَتَرَكْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّمُوْجُ فِىْ بَعْضٍ‌ وَّنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَجَمَعْنٰهُمْ جَمْعًا ۙ‏(99)\nWA TARAKNAA BA’ZAHUM YAWMA-EZINY YAMOOJO FEE BA’ZINW WA NOFEKHA FIS SOORE FAJAMA’NAAHUM JAM-A’NW.\nAnd We will let some of them, that day, to dash (like the billows) one another and the Trumpet will be blown, then will We gather them all together,\nوَّعَرَضْنَا جَهَنَّمَ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَرْضَا ۙ‏(100)\nWA A’RAZNAA JAHANNAMA YAWMA-EZIL LIL-KAAFEREENA A’RZAANIL.\nAnd We will present the hell that day, for the disbelievers, fully exposed to their view,\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ كَانَتْ اَعْيُنُهُمْ فِىْ غِطَآءٍ عَنْ ذِكْرِىْ وَكَانُوْا لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَمْعًا‏(101)\nLAZEENA KAANAT A’YONOHUM FEE GHETAAA-IN A’N ZIKREE WA KAANOO LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SAM-A’A.\nThose whose eyes were under a veil from My reminder, and who could not bear to hear.\nاَفَحَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْا عِبَادِىْ مِنْ دُوْنِىْۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ؕ اِنَّاۤ اَعْتَدْنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ نُزُلًا‏(102)\nA-FA-HASEBAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANY YATTAKHEZOO E’BAADEE MIN DOONEE AWLEYAAA-A, INNAA A-A’TADNAA JAHANNAMA LIL-KAAFEREENA NOZOLAA.\nWhat! think those who disbelieve, that they can take My servants as their guardians besides Me? Verily We have got Hell ready for the infidels to be entertained (therein).\nقُلْ هَلْ نُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِالْاَخْسَرِيْنَ اَعْمَالًا ؕ‏(103)\nQUL HAL NONABBE-OKOM BIL-AKHSAREENA A-A’MAALAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Shall We acquaint you of the greatest losers in (their) deeds?\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ ضَلَّ سَعْيُهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ يَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ يُحْسِنُوْنَ صُنْعًا‏(104)\nALLAZEENA ZALLA SA’-YOHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA HUM YAHSABOONA ANNAHUM YOHSENOONA SUN-A’A.\n(They are) those whose labour is lost in the life of this world and they deem that that they were acquiring good by their deeds.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَلِقَآئِهٖ فَحَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فَلَا نُقِيْمُ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَزْنًا‏(105)\nOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM WA LEQAAA-EHI FA-HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FALAA NOQEEMO LAHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE WAZNAA.\nThese are they who disbelieve in the signs of their Lord and meeting Him so vain will be their deeds, nor will We on the Day of Judgment, assign unto them any weight.\nذٰلِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ بِمَا كَفَرُوْا وَاتَّخَذُوْۤا اٰيٰتِىْ وَرُسُلِىْ هُزُوًا‏(106)\nZAALEKA JAZAAA-OHUM JAHANNAMO BEMAA KAFAROO WAT-TAKHAZOO AAYAATEE WA ROSOLEE HOZOWAA.\nThus Hell is the recompense for what they disbelieved and held My signs and My Apostles with scorn.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ الْفِرْدَوْسِ نُزُلًا ۙ‏(107)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE KAANAT LAHUM JANNAATUL FIRDAWSE NOZOLAA.\nVerily those who believe and do good there is for them the gardens of Paradise for their entertainment,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا لَا يَبْغُوْنَ عَنْهَا حِوَلًا‏(108)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA LAA YABGHOONA A’NHAA HEWALAA.\nAbiding therein, desiring not to be removed therefrom.\nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ الْبَحْرُ مِدَادًا لِّكَلِمٰتِ رَبِّىْ لَنَفِدَ الْبَحْرُ قَبْلَ اَنْ تَنْفَدَ كَلِمٰتُ رَبِّىْ وَلَوْ جِئْنَا بِمِثْلِهٖ مَدَدًا‏(109)\nQUL LAW KAANAL BAHRO MEDAADAL LE-KALEMAATE RABBEE LA-NAFEDAL BAHRO QABLA AN TANFADA KALEMAATO RABBEE WA LAW JE-NAA BE-MISHLEHI MADADAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Should the sea become ink (to write) the words of My Lord, the sea will certainly be exhausted ere the words of my Lord are exhausted, and though we bring the like of that (the seas) to add thereto.\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ اَنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌  ۚ فَمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُوْالِقَآءَ رَبِّهٖ فَلْيَعْمَلْ عَمَلًا صَالِحًاوَّلَايُشْرِكْ بِعِبَادَةِ رَبِّهٖۤ اَحَدًا‏(110)\nQUL INNAMAA ANAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YOOHAA ELAYYA ANNAMAA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUNW WAAHEDUN FAMAN KAANA YARJOO LEQAAA-A RABBEHI FAL-YA’-MAL A’MALAN SAALEHANW WA LAA YUSHRIK BE-E’BAADATE RABBEHI AHADAA.\n(And) say thou: “I am only a man like you, it is revealed unto me that your God is but One God, whosoever therefore desireth to meet his Lord, let him do good deeds, and associate not any one in the worship of His Lord.",
  "merits": "This Surah has 110 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites this Surah will be protected from fitna (evil) for eight days. If a person recites the last verse of Surah al-Kahf before sleeping at night, Allah (s.w.t.) creates a noor (light) from his sleeping place up to the Holy Ka’bah and in this light are angels who continually pray for the reciter until he wakes up.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that if a person wishes to wake up at a particular time, he should recite the last ayah of this Surah and then make the intention that he will wake up at a certain time and he will wake up at that time. He (a.s.) also said that if a person recites this Surah every Thursday night, he will die the death of a martyr. Keeping this Surah (written) in the house becomes a means of protection from poverty and debts."
